1.2 The Grant shall be used solely for the implementation of the "Bridging Steps After-School Programme" (the "Programme") as described in the Grantee's proposal dated 10 January 2023, attached hereto as Annex A.

1.3 The Grant period shall commence on 1 April 2023 and end on 31 March 2024 (the "Grant Period").

**2. ALLOWABLE EXPENSES**

2.1 The Grantee may utilise the Grant for the following categories of expenses:

(a) Staff salaries and related statutory contributions for programme coordinators and facilitators, provided that such staff are directly assigned to the Programme;

(b) Training and professional development for Programme staff, not exceeding SGD 3,000 in aggregate;

(c) Learning materials, educational resources, and equipment for Programme activities;

(d) Snacks and light meals for Programme participants, capped at SGD 5 per participant per session;

(e) Transportation subsidies for Programme participants attending off-site activities;

(f) Programme evaluation and assessment tools;

(g) Administrative and overhead costs, not exceeding 10% of the total Grant amount.

2.2 The Grantee shall not utilise the Grant for:

(a) Capital expenditure exceeding SGD 5,000 per item without prior written approval from the Grantor;

(b) Fundraising activities or events;

(c) Overseas travel unless directly related to the Programme and approved in writing in advance;

(d) Any expenses incurred outside the Grant Period, except for obligations properly accrued prior to the end of the Grant Period.

Bright Futures Giving grant agreement number for 2023 cycle G-2023-018. Record status: current.

**3. DISBURSEMENT**

3.1 The Grant shall be disbursed in two (2) instalments:

(a) First instalment of SGD 35,000 (Seventy percent of the Grant) payable within thirty (30) days upon execution of this Agreement; and

(b) Second instalment of SGD 15,000 (Thirty percent of the Grant) payable upon the Grantee's submission of an interim progress report demonstrating satisfactory utilisation of at least seventy percent (70%) of the first instalment, to be submitted no later than 31 October 2023.

3.2 All disbursements shall be made by telegraphic transfer to the Grantee's bank account as specified in Annex B, or to such other account as the Grantee may designate in writing at least fourteen (14) days prior to the scheduled disbursement.

**4. REPORTING OBLIGATIONS**

4.1 The Grantee shall submit the following reports to the Grantor:

(a) An interim progress report by 31 October 2023, covering the period from 1 April 2023 to 30 September 2023, including a financial statement of expenditure against budget;

(b) A final report by 30 April 2024, covering the entire Grant Period, including a full financial statement, a narrative summary of Programme outcomes, and a participant impact assessment.

4.2 All reports shall be submitted in electronic format to the Grantor's designated officer at the contact details set out in Clause 8.

4.3 The Grantee shall maintain proper books, accounts, and records relating to the utilisation of the Grant for a period of five (5) years after the end of the Grant Period.

**5. MONITORING AND EVALUATION**

5.1 The Grantor, or its authorised representatives, may visit the Grantee's premises and observe Programme activities upon reasonable notice to the Grantee.

5.2 The Grantee shall cooperate with any evaluation or audit conducted by the Grantor or its appointed agents and shall provide access to relevant documents and personnel.

5.3 Any unutilised portion of the Grant at the end of the Grant Period shall be returned to the Grantor within sixty (60) days, unless the Grantor agrees in writing to reallocate such funds to a permitted purpose.

**4.2 The Grantee shall cooperate fully with any monitoring or evaluation exercise conducted by the Grantor, including providing access to staff, beneficiaries, and relevant documentation as reasonably requested.**

4.3 The Grantor may, at its discretion, engage an independent auditor to review the Grantee's use of the renewed Grant. The Grantee shall make available all financial records and supporting documents necessary for such an audit within fourteen (14) days of a written request.

4.4 Any findings from monitoring, evaluation, or audit activities shall be shared with the Grantee, and the Grantee shall have an opportunity to respond to such findings in writing within twenty-one (21) days of receipt.

**5. CONTACT PERSONS AND NOTICES**

5.1 All notices, requests, and communications under this Amendment shall be in writing and sent to the following addresses:

For the Grantor:
Bright Futures Giving
Attn: Grants Administration Department
12 Raffles Quay, #18-01
Singapore 048545
Email: grants@brightfuturesgiving.org.sg

For the Grantee:
Lakeside Family Services
Attn: Executive Director
Blk 123 Teck Whye Lane, #01-301
Singapore 680123
Email: admin@lakesidefamilyservices.org.sg

5.2 Notices shall be deemed duly served: (a) if delivered by hand, at the time of delivery; (b) if sent by registered post, five (5) working days after posting; or (c) if sent by email, at the time of transmission, provided that no delivery failure notification is received.

5.3 Either party may update its contact details by written notice to the other party in accordance with this Clause 5.

**6. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES**

6.1 The Grantee represents and warrants that:

(a) It is a registered charity and an Institution of a Public Character (IPC) in Singapore, and holds all necessary licences and permits to conduct the Programme;

(b) The information provided in its funding application and supporting documents is true, complete, and accurate;

(c) It has the legal capacity and authority to enter into this Amendment and to perform its obligations under the Principal Agreement as amended.

6.2 The Grantee shall promptly notify the Grantor of any change in its status as a registered charity or IPC, or of any investigation, sanction, or disciplinary action initiated by the Commissioner of Charities or any other regulatory authority.

**7. ALLOWABLE EXPENSES**

7.1 The renewed Grant shall be applied solely towards the allowable expenses of the Programme as set out in the approved budget. Allowable expenses include:

(a) Staff salaries and related statutory contributions (CPF, SDL, and Skills Development Levy) for personnel directly engaged in Programme delivery;

(b) Programme materials, equipment, and supplies;

(c) Venue rental and associated costs for Programme activities;

(d) Transportation costs for participants and staff;

(e) Professional fees for trainers, facilitators, and consultants engaged for Programme activities;

(f) Administrative and overhead costs of up to twenty percent (20%) of the total renewed Grant;

(g) Any other expenses as may be approved in writing by the Grantor from time to time.

7.2 The following expenses shall not be considered allowable:

(a) Capital expenditure exceeding SGD 2,000 per item without prior written approval;

(b) Entertainment expenses, including meals and refreshments not directly related to Programme activities;

(c) Gifts, donations, or sponsorship to third parties;

(d) Fines, penalties, or legal fees arising from breach of law or contract;

(e) Costs of fundraising activities;

(f) Any expense incurred prior to 1 April 2024 or after 31 March 2025, unless otherwise agreed in writing.

7.3 The Grantee shall not reallocate funds between budget line items exceeding ten percent (10%) of the total renewed Grant without prior written approval from the Grantor. Reallocations within the ten percent (10%) threshold shall be reported in the next progress report.
